Prerequisites
Windows 10 / 11 (or Windows Server)
PowerShell 5.1+
Administrator privileges
Internet access (or offline files prepared)
Logging tools (recommended):
Sysmon
Wazuh agent

Step 1: Open PowerShell as Administrator
Click Start
Search PowerShell
Right-click → Run as Administrator

Step 2: Allow Script Execution (Temporary)
Set-ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Scope Process -Force

Step 3: Install NuGet Provider (if required)
Install-PackageProvider -Name NuGet -MinimumVersion 2.8.5.201 -Force

Step 4: Install Invoke-AtomicRedTeam Module
Install-Module Invoke-AtomicRedTeam -Scope CurrentUser -Force

Step 5: Install Atomic Test Repository
Install-AtomicRedTeam -GetAtomics

Default install location:
C:\AtomicRedTeam

Step 6: Import the Module
Import-Module Invoke-AtomicRedTeam

Step 7: Verify Installation
Get-Command Invoke-AtomicTest

Expected output:
CommandType: Function
Name: Invoke-AtomicTest

Step 8: Run a Test (Safe Example)
Invoke-AtomicTest T1059 -TestNumbers 1

Step 9: Validate Logs
After running a test, verify detection in:

Windows Logs
Event Viewer → Security
Event ID 4688 (process creation)
Sysmon Logs
Event ID 1 (process creation)
SIEM
Check alerts in Wazuh dashboard

Troubleshooting
# Module not found
## Import-Module Invoke-AtomicRedTeam
# Execution policy error
## Set-ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned -Scope CurrentUser
# No internet / NuGet failure
## Enable NAT or internet access

Verify DNS:
Test-NetConnection google.com -Port 443

Security Notes
Do NOT run in production environments
Use isolated lab VMs
Take snapshots before running tests
Keep Defender enabled with exclusions if needed

